pping one piece (D6), but it places a piece on column 7, which is outside the central box. It is less positionally sound than C3.\n\nReason: The move at (C, 3) is strategically superior because it is the only valid move contained entirely within the central 4x4 box. It follows the strategy of "evaporation" (minimizing the number of opponent pieces flipped early in the game) by flipping only one piece. This preserves my future move options and forces the opponent to play to the outside, whereas moves like B4 or B5 expose my pieces to the edges prematurely.\n\nAnswer: (C, 3)'}
